; relief (docs/ART.md 5.3). Hills: chorographic humps, a two-row lit crest over the west two thirds
; with short hachures under it, a dark checkered flank (q/1) with a void contour down the dark side
; and under the flank, the lit body left open so the ground shows through; keyed in grass colours
; (crest O, o; flank q, 1) and remapped per terrain by the manifest; never mirrored (ground.js), so
; the light stays in the north-west. Peaks: jagged masses, lit west face 4/5/6 with a 7 ridge, shadow
; face 3/2 with 1 hatching, void outline; snow caps 8/7, f; a moonlit edge (6, bone 7 on snow peaks)
; runs down the west side of each massif to its dissolving feet, where it fades to ash 5.

